# Read by /etc/init.d/S50dropbear before it starts the SSH server.
#
# -B  accept a login to an account whose password is blank
#
# A fresh image has no root password and SSH is the only door on the
# network, so without -B the first login would need a serial console.
# dropbear takes this path only while the password field is empty: once
# "passwd" has set one, it asks for it. There is nothing to switch back.
#
# Until then anyone who can reach the device can log in as root, so set a
# password before the device goes on a network you do not control.
DROPBEAR_ARGS="-B"
